! <solver:p610_t3>
! Minimal 2-element split-square T3 patch test (regression sample for the
! `nafems_le1_t3_distorted_smoke` failure that turned out to be a .dat header
! typo: nels-line had `nn=3` for a mesh that actually defined 4 nodes, so the
! coordinate reader consumed connectivity bytes -> stack-buffer-overrun
! (exit code 0xC0000409). Keep this file tiny and committed so anyone running
! `tools/run_le1_min_repro.ps1` can spot a regression in seconds.
!
! Geometry (unit square split along the diagonal 1->3):
!   1 = (0, 0), 2 = (1, 0), 3 = (1, 1), 4 = (0, 1)
!   E1: 1-2-3   (lower-right triangle)
!   E2: 1-3-4   (upper-left triangle)
!
! Loading: uniaxial sigma = [-100, 0, 0] kPa via tractions on the two right
!   and two left edges of the square (top / bottom edges carry no traction
!   because their outward normal is perpendicular to sigma_x).
!     edge 2->3 (right):   n = ( 1,  0), T = sigma . n = (-100, 0)
!     edge 4->1 (left):    n = (-1,  0), T = sigma . n = ( 100, 0)
!
! Closed-form (plane strain, nu = 0.25, tension-positive):
!   sxx = -100, syy = 0, txy = 0, szz = nu*(sxx+syy) = -25
!
! BCs (rigid-body motion only):
!   node 1: fix x and y
!   node 2: fix y
!   node 4: fix x
! <BEGIN:AnalysisOptions>
! failure_criterion MohrCoulomb
! material_type Isotropic
! mesh_type T3
! solver_executable p610_t3_elastoplastic
! expected_sxx_kPa -100
! expected_syy_kPa 0
! expected_txy_kPa 0
! expected_szz_kPa -25
! tolerance_kPa 1e-3
! <END:AnalysisOptions>
2  4  1
89  1.0e10  0  0  1000000  0.25  0
0  0
1  0
1  1
0  1
1  2  3
1  3  4
3
1  0  0
2  1  0
4  0  1
4
1  2  3  4
0.0001  80  3  0
1
0  -100  0  0
2
2  3
4  1
